WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.369
There are so many new
beauty releases happening

00:00:02.369 --> 00:00:04.204
all the time, so we gathered some of the

00:00:04.204 --> 00:00:06.473
most-hyped products to test for ourselves.

00:00:06.473 --> 00:00:08.708
I've never tried a Plouise product before,

00:00:08.708 --> 00:00:10.543
but I kept seeing this blush everywhere.

00:00:10.543 --> 00:00:12.445
It's The Cheek of It liquid blush.

00:00:12.445 --> 00:00:14.114
The formula is actually water-based,

00:00:14.114 --> 00:00:16.383
so it did blend into
my skin really easily.

00:00:16.383 --> 00:00:18.084
I think maybe because it's water-based,

00:00:18.084 --> 00:00:20.820
it wasn't as pigmented
as I expected it to be.

00:00:20.820 --> 00:00:23.189
I did add quite a bit more
to build up the color,

00:00:23.189 --> 00:00:24.457
but I think it turned out pretty,

00:00:24.457 --> 00:00:27.360
and it didn't move any of
the product I already had on.

00:00:27.360 --> 00:00:28.762
Even though I liked the end result,

00:00:28.762 --> 00:00:30.997
I think I've tried better liquid blushes.

00:00:30.997 --> 00:00:33.233
This lipstick keeps
selling out everywhere,

00:00:33.233 --> 00:00:35.468
but I finally got my
hands on a couple shades.

00:00:35.468 --> 00:00:39.272
This is the Revlon Super
Lustrous Glass Shine lipstick.

00:00:39.272 --> 00:00:41.941
It's one of those lipsticks
that kind of mimics a gloss,

00:00:41.941 --> 00:00:44.411
so you get this really
pretty sheer wash of color

00:00:44.411 --> 00:00:46.212
and that high-shine finish.

00:00:46.212 --> 00:00:49.382
These are beautiful and
feel so good on the lips,

00:00:49.382 --> 00:00:50.850
so I totally get the hype.

00:00:50.850 --> 00:00:53.286
They actually remind me of
the Hourglass glossy balms,

00:00:53.286 --> 00:00:55.488
except these are, like, $20 cheaper.

00:00:55.488 --> 00:00:57.824
Miss A is that website
where all of the makeup

00:00:57.824 --> 00:00:59.192
is super affordable.

00:00:59.192 --> 00:01:02.162
I saw people raving about
their AOA Plush Blush,

00:01:02.162 --> 00:01:03.463
so I had to try it.

00:01:03.463 --> 00:01:05.932
The packaging is literally
like a nail polish,

00:01:05.932 --> 00:01:07.867
so it just felt a little odd applying,

00:01:07.867 --> 00:01:09.836
but I was really impressed with this.

00:01:09.836 --> 00:01:12.572
It's a gel formula, so it's
more like a cheek stain

00:01:12.572 --> 00:01:13.940
that feels lightweight.

00:01:13.940 --> 00:01:17.277
These blend out so easily,
and they are very pigmented.

00:01:17.277 --> 00:01:18.912
I really, really love these.

00:01:18.912 --> 00:01:22.515
I also picked up the new AOA
Flaw Eraser foundation sticks.

00:01:22.515 --> 00:01:24.050
I got a few shades so I could bronze

00:01:24.050 --> 00:01:25.819
and highlight with these as well.

00:01:25.819 --> 00:01:27.587
I got nervous about how
these were going to look

00:01:27.587 --> 00:01:30.690
on my skin when I was applying,
because they felt thick,

00:01:30.690 --> 00:01:32.792
but once I started blending
it out with my brush

00:01:32.792 --> 00:01:35.061
and I picked up the extra
product with my sponge,

00:01:35.061 --> 00:01:36.729
it was so much better.

00:01:36.729 --> 00:01:39.499
I wasn't expecting these
to be so full coverage.

00:01:39.499 --> 00:01:41.000
It is more of a matte formula,

00:01:41.000 --> 00:01:43.369
but I don't think it
made my skin look dry.

00:01:43.369 --> 00:01:44.704
And all of my other products

00:01:44.704 --> 00:01:46.239
went on top of this just fine.

00:01:46.239 --> 00:01:49.109
I can't believe both of
these products are under $2.

00:01:49.109 --> 00:01:50.443
Charlotte Tilbury just released

00:01:50.443 --> 00:01:53.613
this Hollywood Glow Glide
Face Architect highlighter.

00:01:53.613 --> 00:01:55.615
I got the shade Pillow Talk Glow.

00:01:55.615 --> 00:01:58.284
It's supposed to give this
sort of soft-focus glow,

00:01:58.284 --> 00:02:00.120
rather than be super glittery.

00:02:00.120 --> 00:02:02.522
It also has emollients in
it to hydrate the skin,

00:02:02.522 --> 00:02:03.823
which, I don't think I've ever tried

00:02:03.823 --> 00:02:05.859
a hydrating powder highlighter.

00:02:05.859 --> 00:02:08.128
I'm torn on this product
because from afar,

00:02:08.128 --> 00:02:10.330
I think it looks really
beautiful, but up close,

00:02:10.330 --> 00:02:12.632
I feel like it made my
skin look a bit textured.

00:02:12.632 --> 00:02:14.901
To be fair, my skin
hasn't been great lately.

00:02:14.901 --> 00:02:15.969
It's been really dry,

00:02:15.969 --> 00:02:17.370
and I've been getting little breakouts,

00:02:17.370 --> 00:02:20.273
so highlighter is probably the
last thing I need right now.

00:02:20.273 --> 00:02:21.774
I do think this is really pretty.

00:02:21.774 --> 00:02:23.009
I just don't think it works great

00:02:23.009 --> 00:02:24.577
if you already have texture.

00:02:24.577 --> 00:02:26.479
I don't think I've purchased
a CoverGirl product

00:02:26.479 --> 00:02:29.649
since high school, but these
glosses were calling my name.

00:02:29.649 --> 00:02:31.284
This is the new Yummy Gloss.

00:02:31.284 --> 00:02:33.186
These smell incredible.

00:02:33.186 --> 00:02:36.022
The pinky-clear one
smells like a piña colada,

00:02:36.022 --> 00:02:38.458
and the more burgundy
one smells like berries.

00:02:38.458 --> 00:02:39.926
The scents really took me back

00:02:39.926 --> 00:02:42.295
to, like, old-school Lip Smackers.

00:02:42.295 --> 00:02:44.364
They have this huge doe-foot applicator,

00:02:44.364 --> 00:02:47.901
which I'm a fan of, and they
feel so good on the lips,

00:02:47.901 --> 00:02:50.203
super shiny and not sticky at all.

00:02:50.203 --> 00:02:52.906
I do have to mention that
the product description

00:02:52.906 --> 00:02:54.941
doesn't say this is a plumping gloss,

00:02:54.941 --> 00:02:56.676
but I got this tingly feeling

00:02:56.676 --> 00:02:58.444
on my lips when I applied it.

00:02:58.444 --> 00:03:00.213
I don't know if it's
because it is plumping

00:03:00.213 --> 00:03:02.115
and they just weren't
super clear about that

00:03:02.115 --> 00:03:03.950
or if I'm allergic to something in it,

00:03:03.950 --> 00:03:06.152
but either way, just had to let you know.

00:03:06.152 --> 00:03:08.154
Made by Mitchell released powder versions

00:03:08.154 --> 00:03:10.089
of its liquid Blurshes and bronzers.

00:03:10.089 --> 00:03:12.559
I'm not saying blush weird,
that's just what they're called.

00:03:12.559 --> 00:03:15.228
I do have to say I'm not
a fan of the packaging,

00:03:15.228 --> 00:03:17.897
just because it's not
an easy shape to store.

00:03:17.897 --> 00:03:20.600
But on to the actual products
inside the packaging,

00:03:20.600 --> 00:03:22.735
the pigment on these is unreal.

00:03:22.735 --> 00:03:24.370
I tapped my brush off a lot,

00:03:24.370 --> 00:03:26.639
and I still got full color payoff.

00:03:26.639 --> 00:03:28.942
This powder formula is
still easy to blend, though.

00:03:28.942 --> 00:03:30.510
It was easy to diffuse the color

00:03:30.510 --> 00:03:33.213
without it getting patchy
or ruining my foundation.

00:03:33.213 --> 00:03:35.415
They just look really smooth on the skin.

00:03:35.415 --> 00:03:36.516
I love these.

00:03:36.516 --> 00:03:39.085
ELF recently released a
line of color correctors.

00:03:39.085 --> 00:03:41.788
I picked up the peach shade
to brighten up my under-eyes.

00:03:41.788 --> 00:03:45.024
This formula is really
creamy and easy to work with.

00:03:45.024 --> 00:03:46.960
I was worried it was almost too peach

00:03:46.960 --> 00:03:48.061
when I was applying it,

00:03:48.061 --> 00:03:51.331
but my concealer blended on
top of this really nicely.

00:03:51.331 --> 00:03:52.932
It actually did add some brightness,

00:03:52.932 --> 00:03:55.368
and you cannot beat that $4 price point.

00:03:55.368 --> 00:03:57.604
Makeup by Mario has finally released

00:03:57.604 --> 00:04:00.373
its long-awaited SurrealSkin foundation.

00:04:00.373 --> 00:04:03.042
Looking at it in the
bottle, it looked glittery.

00:04:03.042 --> 00:04:04.978
I think because there's mica in it.

00:04:04.978 --> 00:04:07.380
The formula itself feels slightly thick,

00:04:07.380 --> 00:04:10.183
but it did feel weightless
once I applied it to my face.

00:04:10.183 --> 00:04:11.651
This covers a lot.

00:04:11.651 --> 00:04:13.987
Like, I couldn't see
any of my discoloration

00:04:13.987 --> 00:04:15.421
or acne through this.

00:04:15.421 --> 00:04:16.889
I do think that this foundation

00:04:16.889 --> 00:04:18.524
did enhance my texture, though.

00:04:18.524 --> 00:04:19.926
I mentioned in my last video

00:04:19.926 --> 00:04:22.028
that my skin hasn't been great lately,

00:04:22.028 --> 00:04:25.331
but I still do good skin
prep before foundation.

00:04:25.331 --> 00:04:28.001
This just kind of highlighted
those problem areas.

00:04:28.001 --> 00:04:31.037
I do think it worked well
with all of my other products.

00:04:31.037 --> 00:04:33.172
I want to try this again
once my skin texture

00:04:33.172 --> 00:04:35.508
gets a little better, because
the coverage is great,

00:04:35.508 --> 00:04:37.877
but I'm not 100% sold on this.

00:04:37.877 --> 00:04:40.913
This is the Kaleidos
Mono blush in Dreamwalk.

00:04:40.913 --> 00:04:44.150
This kind of blue-based
pink, almost lilac color

00:04:44.150 --> 00:04:46.386
has been so popular lately.

00:04:46.386 --> 00:04:48.788
I was worried that it would
look weird on my skin tone,

00:04:48.788 --> 00:04:50.823
but I actually thought this was so pretty.

00:04:50.823 --> 00:04:53.559
This formula is so silky smooth.

00:04:53.559 --> 00:04:55.028
It blends out beautifully,

00:04:55.028 --> 00:04:56.963
and the pigment was on the softer side

00:04:56.963 --> 00:04:59.532
but totally buildable
and easy to work with.

00:04:59.532 --> 00:05:02.001
I like this color way more
than I thought I would.

00:05:02.001 --> 00:05:04.804
These are the Kiss
imPress press-on falsies.

00:05:04.804 --> 00:05:07.440
So these are press-on
lashes that don't need glue,

00:05:07.440 --> 00:05:09.575
and you apply them underneath your lashes

00:05:09.575 --> 00:05:12.045
instead of above, so
it looks more natural.

00:05:12.045 --> 00:05:14.447
I'm not gonna lie, I had
a really difficult time

00:05:14.447 --> 00:05:17.116
figuring these out. I
don't wear falsies often,

00:05:17.116 --> 00:05:19.252
so I'm already not great at applying them,

00:05:19.252 --> 00:05:22.355
but this application
process felt so much harder.

00:05:22.355 --> 00:05:24.057
Because you apply them below the lashes,

00:05:24.057 --> 00:05:25.792
it made my eyes water, which in turn

00:05:25.792 --> 00:05:28.027
made the lashes not stick very well.

00:05:28.027 --> 00:05:30.296
I tried pressing them
together with my real lashes

00:05:30.296 --> 00:05:32.365
using the tweezers and my fingers,

00:05:32.365 --> 00:05:34.500
but they didn't feel secure at all.

00:05:34.500 --> 00:05:37.003
If I blinked too fast,
they would just pop off.

00:05:37.003 --> 00:05:38.338
These have a lot of great reviews,

00:05:38.338 --> 00:05:39.906
so they just might not be right for me

00:05:39.906 --> 00:05:41.207
and my sensitive eyes.

00:05:41.207 --> 00:05:42.642
I just think applying falsies

00:05:42.642 --> 00:05:44.577
with glue feels a lot more secure.

00:05:44.577 --> 00:05:46.813
This is the REM Beauty Midnight Shadows

00:05:46.813 --> 00:05:49.549
lustrous liquid eyeshadow
in the shade Fembot.

00:05:49.549 --> 00:05:51.250
I've tried out this formula before,

00:05:51.250 --> 00:05:54.654
but this shade in particular
is having a moment on TikTok.

00:05:54.654 --> 00:05:56.556
It's this sheer pinky-nude color

00:05:56.556 --> 00:05:59.092
with a bunch of iridescent
blue sparkles in it.

00:05:59.092 --> 00:06:01.728
It's really beautiful
and shifty on the eyes.

00:06:01.728 --> 00:06:03.463
I do think the best way to apply it

00:06:03.463 --> 00:06:04.831
is with your fingers.

00:06:04.831 --> 00:06:06.566
This formula does dry down quickly,

00:06:06.566 --> 00:06:07.934
but it looks so cool,

00:06:07.934 --> 00:06:10.436
and it doesn't settle in
the creases of my lids.

00:06:10.436 --> 00:06:12.872
ELF just released these
O Face satin lipsticks,

00:06:12.872 --> 00:06:14.707
so I picked up a couple shades.

00:06:14.707 --> 00:06:17.076
I'm just gonna say it.
These are incredible.

00:06:17.076 --> 00:06:19.812
They are so creamy and
comfortable on the lips.

00:06:19.812 --> 00:06:22.648
They just glide on, and
the pigment is unreal.

00:06:22.648 --> 00:06:25.518
Like, these are one-swipe
lipsticks for $9.

00:06:25.518 --> 00:06:27.820
They are a satin lipstick,
so they do transfer,

00:06:27.820 --> 00:06:29.555
but they are so good.

00:06:29.555 --> 00:06:31.324
I've been really excited to try this

00:06:31.324 --> 00:06:33.960
Urban Decay Quickie 24-hour multiuse

00:06:33.960 --> 00:06:36.262
hydrating full-coverage concealer.

00:06:36.262 --> 00:06:38.931
It's huge, and it has a
brush attached on top.

00:06:38.931 --> 00:06:40.500
This shade was a little too dark for me,

00:06:40.500 --> 00:06:42.001
but I tried to make it work.

00:06:42.001 --> 00:06:43.836
I applied it in all the areas I normally

00:06:43.836 --> 00:06:45.905
apply concealer, and
I usually like to wait

00:06:45.905 --> 00:06:47.940
a couple minutes before I blend it out,

00:06:47.940 --> 00:06:50.710
but this one dries down very fast.

00:06:50.710 --> 00:06:52.478
I did have a bit of trouble blending,

00:06:52.478 --> 00:06:55.515
but I was immediately impressed
by the coverage this gives.

00:06:55.515 --> 00:06:57.350
I also think this brush is actually good,

00:06:57.350 --> 00:06:59.285
but I think the bristles are too short.

00:06:59.285 --> 00:07:00.386
I do think it's interesting

00:07:00.386 --> 00:07:02.622
that it's described as
a hydrating concealer,

00:07:02.622 --> 00:07:05.425
because to me it leans
more natural to matte.

00:07:05.425 --> 00:07:07.760
But this is a really good
full-coverage concealer.

00:07:07.760 --> 00:07:09.595
We have a new product from Rare Beauty.

00:07:09.595 --> 00:07:11.998
This is the Positive Light
under-eye brightener.

00:07:11.998 --> 00:07:13.533
It has this metal applicator

00:07:13.533 --> 00:07:15.768
that's supposed to be
cooling for the under-eyes.

00:07:15.768 --> 00:07:17.303
I blended this out with my fingers,

00:07:17.303 --> 00:07:18.938
and the coverage is definitely sheer,

00:07:18.938 --> 00:07:20.540
but I do think it brightened.

00:07:20.540 --> 00:07:22.975
I added a little more, and
it does build up nicely

00:07:22.975 --> 00:07:24.610
while still feeling weightless.

00:07:24.610 --> 00:07:26.112
I applied my concealer on top,

00:07:26.112 --> 00:07:27.547
and it blended out just fine.

00:07:27.547 --> 00:07:29.549
I think this formula layers really well,

00:07:29.549 --> 00:07:32.018
and even though the brightening
is on the more subtle side,

00:07:32.018 --> 00:07:33.853
I can definitely see a difference.

00:07:33.853 --> 00:07:37.056
This is the Dior Addict Lip
Maximizer plumping gloss.

00:07:37.056 --> 00:07:39.792
This gloss looks so glittery and beautiful

00:07:39.792 --> 00:07:41.894
in every single video
I've ever seen of it,

00:07:41.894 --> 00:07:44.630
but unfortunately, I didn't like it.

00:07:44.630 --> 00:07:46.332
The applicator is pretty small,

00:07:46.332 --> 00:07:47.900
especially by today's standards,

00:07:47.900 --> 00:07:49.869
but that's not my biggest issue with it.

00:07:49.869 --> 00:07:51.037
It's the glitter.

00:07:51.037 --> 00:07:53.206
The glitter in this
feels gritty on the lips.

00:07:53.206 --> 00:07:54.740
Like, when I rub my lips together,

00:07:54.740 --> 00:07:56.609
I can feel all that glitter,

00:07:56.609 --> 00:07:59.745
and the plumping aspect
was, like, nonexistent.

00:07:59.745 --> 00:08:01.948
I saw and felt zero plumping.

00:08:01.948 --> 00:08:03.749
I wanted to love it
because it looks pretty,

00:08:03.749 --> 00:08:06.052
but in my opinion, it's so not worth it.

00:08:06.052 --> 00:08:09.622
Let's talk about the L'Oréal
Telescopic Lift mascara.

00:08:09.622 --> 00:08:10.990
It has what they describe as

00:08:10.990 --> 00:08:12.558
a "double-hook bristle brush,"

00:08:12.558 --> 00:08:15.962
which is supposed to give you
an instant lift and volume.

00:08:15.962 --> 00:08:17.296
I asked my editor, Natalie,

00:08:17.296 --> 00:08:19.866
to show the full application
process with no cuts,

00:08:19.866 --> 00:08:22.735
so you can see how this
mascara actually performs.

00:08:22.735 --> 00:08:25.238
I do really like how it
makes my lashes look,

00:08:25.238 --> 00:08:27.373
but the brush is not my favorite.

00:08:27.373 --> 00:08:30.176
It picks up a ridiculous
amount of product.

00:08:30.176 --> 00:08:32.411
Look how much product I
scraped off the brush.

00:08:32.411 --> 00:08:34.614
I felt like I spent most
of the time applying

00:08:34.614 --> 00:08:36.382
just trying to remove excess product

00:08:36.382 --> 00:08:37.850
so it wouldn't look clumpy.

00:08:37.850 --> 00:08:39.352
I also got the waterproof version,

00:08:39.352 --> 00:08:42.188
and I found this formula
a lot easier to control.

00:08:42.188 --> 00:08:44.423
I think I prefer the waterproof version.

00:08:44.423 --> 00:08:45.625
I wouldn't say this mascara

00:08:45.625 --> 00:08:47.260
makes it look like I'm wearing falsies,

00:08:47.260 --> 00:08:48.861
but it definitely gives me a lot

00:08:48.861 --> 00:08:51.330
of length and lift, and
I will keep using it.

